A||||14||saleenfiero||Your thoughts on Nissan Pulsars???||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||09-04-2001||08:24 PM||||I know I am probably asking for it here, but does anyone have any solid info on the 1st gen Pulsar.  I am thinking about buying one for the cold Canadian winters and saving for a new fiero next year.  Anyone got specs?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Neal||09-04-2001||08:48 PM||||I dont have the specs, but a good buddy of mine had one untill he bought a fiero.<P>What i do know there is a single cam and a dual cam version, dual cam is much peppier.<P>It was a decent car, he was happy with it but it was definatly underpowered... handled OK, read not as good as a fiero.<P>my impression with it was good nice car for what is it.  I only drove it once, was on the highway fully loaded with camping gear and the car needed to be down shifted to make it up the hills.  very comfortable though.<P>hope my babbling helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||09-04-2001||10:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>What i do know there is a single cam and a dual cam version, dual cam is much peppier.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I may be wrong but I believe you're thinking of the 2nd generation Pulsar.  The 2nd generation had the removeable tops and hatchback, along with the optional twin cam engine.<P>The first generation Pulsar was the very "boxy wedge-shaped" model.  No T-tops, just a sunroof, and no optional engine.<P>Pulsars had front-wheel drive so they'll work well for those "Canadian winters."  Not much carrying capacity (not that they were meant for that) and the back seat is, well, big enough to carry small objects ... but certainly not people.<P>Reliability was on par with other Japanese cars ... that is, above average.  Not sure on the availability/affordability of parts.<P>HTH ...||||reg||6
Z||000003||saleenfiero||09-04-2001||10:52 PM||||Actually, come to think of it, I'm looking to buy a 2nd gen Pulsar, not a 1st.  Those first gen ones are hideous!||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||09-04-2001||10:53 PM||||Funny you should ask.  I used to have an '86 (1st gen, boxy, wedge-shaped).  Not too fast, but damn reliable.  There was no twin cam available, but there was a turbo option (really).  N/A's were 1.4 liter, mine averaged 28-29 mpg (tuned right) and the turbos were 1.6 liter, and I have no specs on mileage for those.  Mine was an NX, an option package that included sunroof, A/C, auto, rear defrost, and a (surprisingly) nice interior facelift, with embroidered (!)"Pulsar NX" logos on all four seats and embroidered checkerboard pattern.    I miss my old reliable, as the Fiero has been nothing but hell since I bought it.  I have two warnings, tho.  As soon as you find one you like, check the wiring over the alternator bracket.  The bracket had worn through the loom and into some wires which was popping the ECM fuse.  Zip-tied some split heater hose on the bracket and patched the wire, and all was well.  Also, the CV joints are a point of contention, but overall the car is bulletproof.  I sold mine with 167,000 miles showing, original engine, running like new.  Also, given decent tires, they are great in snow, rain and ice.  Enjoy, and feel free to email me with any other questions at gregman_1@excite.com .<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||09-05-2001||12:51 AM||||Three letters: P O S  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||09-05-2001||10:00 AM||||My sister-in-law had one. They were OK cars. Like stated above, not real "performace" orientated, But decent cars. Hers ran fine for the first 100K miles than had some minor problems with wiring like b lo 0 said above. Also she had a problem with the brakes once. (I think it was owner caused) They had to flush out the brake system and refill it. Something about she put in the wrong fluid.<BR>Oh, she also had a problem with mufflers rusting out. Don't know which brand she used but it seems every fall it needed replacing.<P>Depending on overall condition and price, It would make a good second car.<BR>I could only find specs for an 88.<BR>I have no idea if these are "real" but here they are:<BR>Tech specs<BR>Engine..............1.8L 4 cylinder 110hp<BR>0-60mph.............9.5 sec. est.<BR>Top speed...........a little more than 75mph<BR>Fuel milage..........30 mpg on average<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||saleenfiero||09-05-2001||07:11 PM||||Thanx fort the 411.  As you can guess, I'm not looking to buy one of these cars for performance.  I'll leave that to the 2M6.  I'm trying like an SOB to find some info on these damn thing, but there's nowhere on the net it seems to find any info.  Just news on the new australian Pulsar.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||09-05-2001||10:33 PM||||should be kept in garage with Gremlins, Pacers. Not being able to find out anything on them should be a big clue.||||reg||1
Z||000009||b lo 0||09-06-2001||12:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B><BR>Top speed...........a little more than 75mph<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's funny, I got my '86 up to around 120 mph once and above 100 regularly.  (Downhill) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.  And the POS comment, I have had waaaaaay more problems from my Fiero than I ever had with the Pulsar, and the Fiero has 20,000 miles less than the Pulsar.  I almost wish I hadn't of sold it.  The great thing about Nissans, unless you really abuse them, they'll last you forever.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Neal||09-06-2001||12:51 AM||||87ECOS, your right i was thinking about the 2nd gen pulsar's.<P>About them being POS, my buddies had over 300,000 km about 190000 miles and he had very few problems, the car was damn reliable||||reg||1
Z||000011||My7Fieros||09-06-2001||01:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>should be kept in garage with Gremlins, Pacers. Not being able to find out anything on them should be a big clue.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR><B>A-MEN</B> .... "what are my thoughts on a pulsar?", easy, I have NO thoughts about them. If you're looking for a beater or whatever for the winter, I can think of a thousand other cars before a Pulsar. Im sure they were ok cars, being Nissan and all, but they havent made them in years (thank God). I never did like them too much. Get an old Accord or Maxima or something...just my .02 cents worth. <B><FONT SIZE="3"><I><FONT COLOR="orange">7</B></FONT></I></FONT><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||saleenfiero||09-06-2001||06:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR>[b]should be kept in garage with Gremlins, Pacers. Not being able to find out anything on them should be a big clue.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well unless you know where to look, fiero info is pretty tought to come by too.  Do you have some kind of apprehension to them?  I just wanna get some pros and cons.  Its not like they are my favorite cars or anything.  And who the hell would keep a gremlin in the garage anyway?<BR><B>A-MEN</B> .... "what are my thoughts on a pulsar?", easy, I have NO thoughts about them. If you're looking for a beater or whatever for the winter, I can think of a thousand other cars before a Pulsar. Im sure they were ok cars, being Nissan and all, but they havent made them in years (thank God). I never did like them too much. Get an old Accord or Maxima or something...just my .02 cents worth. <B><FONT SIZE="3"><I><FONT COLOR="orange">7</B></FONT></I></FONT><P>[/B][/QUOTE]<BR>Sure they're still making the Pulsar.  The new model just came out this year.  Probably has nothing to do with the old car, but still....<P><P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
